{"tool": "answer", "text": "To get the size of the report.pdf file, use the pdfinfo command with the -f option to specify the first page and the -l option to specify the last page. Since you only want the file size, you can use the following command:

pdfinfo -f 1 -l 1 report.pdf

This will print the file size of the first page of the report.pdf file. The file size is listed under the 'file size' section of the output.", "cite": 1}

{"tool": "answer", "text": "To determine which of your services are currently running, you can use the `systemctl status` command followed by the service name(s) you want to check. For example, running `systemctl status bluetooth` will show the status of the bluetooth service.

Alternatively, to check the status of all services, you can use `systemctl list-units --type=service --state=active`.

This will list all services that are currently active (running).", "cite": 1}
